00:07:51.000 --> 00:08:42.000
These sound like a lot of expectations, and I'm just wondering where they come from. Does it come from an individual family or is it coming from society more broadly? Yes, it is. You know, in communication studies, particularly we're interested in how meaning is made by communicating, communicating with our friends, our family, or the messages we get through our social system. So learning how to do daughtering and learning what daughters should do or what a good daughter is is often coming to us from messages very early in our life. Even when we're a small child, we're looking at our siblings, we're looking at our parent and how they're daughtering

