00:27:45.000 --> 00:28:33.000
So just some recasting of what daughtering can be and some reimagining of what you're already doing well can be a huge shift for women to feel a lot of relief and a lot of camaraderie and solidarity in doing daughtering. And the goal is to get to that part where you like it, where you enjoy it, where you think my family and being part of a family is a benefit and I want to do the work that I need to do to be in the family because I enjoy the benefits that I get from it as well. You published the research article on daughtering during the COVID-19 pandemic. I'm wondering, what did you find? How did the pandemic change women's experience of daughtering?

