but they keep going out to talk to all the neighbors. And so in that study, one of the most interesting things was just realizing that when daughtering and the facets of daughtering and the needs of our parent are made more visible to us, then we can wrap our mind around, what can I do, what can I not do, what am I willing to take under my control that I need to be doing for this parent and what do I have to let go? And so much of being a good daughter has to do with thinking, what am I doing for them, but I also have to protect me. So I have to balance the way that I use and share my resources. And in COVID-19, resources were extremely strained at work with our little families,

